# Service ownership standard

Every production service has one accountable team even when several teams contribute code.

## Tier-1 minimum

A tier-1 service must have:

- a named owning team;
- an availability or correctness SLO;
- actionable dashboards and alerts;
- an on-call escalation path;
- a tested rollback or recovery path;
- a current service page and at least one operational runbook;
- dependency and data-ownership notes sufficient for incident response.

Ownership is not the same as exclusive contribution. [[Webhook Gateway]] is jointly developed, but Platform & Reliability is accountable for its runtime while Core Services owns event semantics.

A service that cannot meet this standard should not be promoted to a critical production dependency without an explicit exception.
